# Test: `ze config validate` refuses a RIR delegation source on plain HTTP off
# the box, and accepts one on the router itself.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-rir-delegation-source-override AC-4 and AC-5.
#            AC-4 -- a source whose scheme is plain HTTP and whose host is not
#                    loopback is refused before any byte is fetched, and the
#                    message names the URL and the rule.
#            AC-5 -- a source whose host is 127.0.0.1 over plain HTTP is
#                    accepted, which is what an on-box mirror needs.
# PREVENTS:  a `ze:validate` that never runs. The leaf's own
#            `pattern "https?://.+"` accepts both URLs below, so only
#            ValidateFetchURL separates them, and it runs only while `system`
#            is one of the sections ValidateCustomSections walks. An annotation
#            outside that list is spelled exactly like one inside it and
#            refuses nothing, which is how the first config here loaded clean
#            until 2026-09-03.
#
# DISCRIMINATOR: drop "system" from validatedSections
# (internal/component/config/validate_sections.go) and step 1 exits 0.

stdin=offbox:terminator=EOF_OFFBOX
system {
	rir {
		delegation-source ripencc {
			url "http://mirror.example.com/delegated-ripencc-extended-latest";
		}
	}
}
EOF_OFFBOX

stdin=onbox:terminator=EOF_ONBOX
system {
	rir {
		delegation-source ripencc {
			url "http://127.0.0.1:8080/delegated-ripencc-extended-latest";
		}
	}
}
EOF_ONBOX

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=offbox
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=delegation source
expect=stdout:contains=mirror.example.com

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=onbox
expect=exit:code=0
